></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAYAMA, YUMIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIJIMA, YOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A catalyst having an activity for removing nitrogen oxides (DeNOx activity) at a low temperature region of 200 to 350  DEG C, which is obtainable by adding, to a platinum-based catalyst, tellurium and also, at least one member selected from among an alkali metal, an alkaline earth metal, boron, zinc, phosphorus, tungsten, molybdenum, tin and cerium and/or a zeolite; and a method for removing nitrogen oxides using the catalyst. A method for maintaining the DeNOx activity of the above catalyst in a wide temperature region of 200 to 600  DEG C which comprises combining the above catalyst with a Ag- or Cu-based catalyst which has high activity at 300  DEG C or more is also disclosed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un catalyseur capable d'extraire des oxydes d'azote (DeNOx) dans une plage de faibles températures comprises entre 200 et 300  DEG C. A un catalyseur à base de platine, on ajoute du télurium et au moins un membre pris dans l'éventail suivant : métal alcalin, métal alcalino-terreux, bore, zinc, phosphore, tungstène, molybdène, étain et cérium et/ou zéolite. L'invention concerne également un procédé d'extraction d'oxydes d'azote au moyen dudit catalyseur. Cette invention porte également sur un procédé qui permet de maintenir une activité DeNOxdu catalyseur susmentionné dans une vaste plage de température comprise entre 200 et 600  DEG C et qui consiste à combiner ce catalyseur avec un autre catalyseur à base d'argent ou de cuivre très actif à 300  DEG C ou plus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>